Idempotent toString', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': 'identical strings on successive calls', 'description': 'Create a Zone, add a few records (e.g., SOA, NS, A). Call toString() twice and verify that both returned strings are exactly equal, proving that toString() does not mutate internal state.'}]}, {'group': 'Zone after removal of a record', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': '"example.org. 3600 IN NS ns1.example.org.\\nexample.org. 3600 IN NS ns2.example.org.\\n"', 'description': 'Add two NS records and one A record, then remove the A record via removeRecord(). The master‑file representation returned by toString() must contain only the two NS lines, confirming that removal is reflected.'}]}, {'group': 'Multiple records of the same name and type (A)', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': '"www.example.com. 300 IN A 192.0.2.1\\nwww.example.com. 300 IN A 192.0.2.2\\n"', 'description': 'Add two A records for the same host name. toString() must emit both lines in the order they were added, demonstrating that the zone stores multiple RRs of the same type.'}]}, {'group': 'Order preservation when mixing addRRset and addRecord', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': '"example.net. 7200 IN MX 10 mail.example.net.\\nexample.net. 7200 IN A 203.0.113.5\\n"', 'description': 'Create an RRset containing an MX record and add it with addRRset(). Then add an A record with addRecord(). toString() must list the MX line first followed by the A line, confirming that insertion order across the two APIs is respected.'}]}, {'group': 'Zero‑TTL record handling', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': '"host.example.org. 0 IN A 198.51.100.7\\n"', 'description': 'Add an A record with a TTL of 0. The master‑file line produced by toString() must contain the literal "0" as the TTL, proving that zero TTLs are serialized correctly.'}]}, {'group': 'Large zone line‑count verification', 'cases': [{'input': [], 'expected': '50 lines', 'description': "Add 50 distinct A records (e.g., host0.example.com